From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:18:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host: the third endless wait that answered a timeout nobody
 asked for
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`sk_idle` is the poll nobody can be woken for — an empty set, or descriptors this service does not
manage — and it slept a 100 ms slice and returned 0 whatever timeout it was given. With `ms < 0` that
is the same lie the other two paths told: a caller that arms itself and expects to be woken reads 0 as
its own deadline expiring, and a transport that does it in the pollset thread spins there instead of
running the work it queued (log DEA255C6 has `poll(1 fds, -1 ms): fd 0 … -> 0` and a dispatcher thread
at ~970 ms/s for the whole session). An endless wait now sleeps in 1 ms slices and re-reads the
teardown hook, and only a real timeout returns.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: the Nextendo online seams are this fork's own work: upstream's multi-worktree tree takes them to seedds/nxnative instead
Issue: https://github.com/GigiFrack/NX2Apple (fork)

---
 dm/host/hle_net.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/hle_net.c b/dm/host/hle_net.c
index 45f6053a..a88fbff2 100644
--- a/dm/host/hle_net.c
+++ b/dm/host/hle_net.c
@@ -82,7 +82,20 @@ int dm_sk_errno(void) { return t_skerr; }
 #define SKF(m, cname, ...) HLE_FORCE(m, "local BSD descriptor service; remote networking unavailable", int, cname, __VA_ARGS__)
 void dm_guest_sleep_ns(int64_t ns);
 void dm_guest_cond_wait_ns(pthread_cond_t *c, pthread_mutex_t *m, int64_t ns);
-static int sk_idle(int64_t ms) { dm_guest_sleep_ns((ms < 0 ? 100 : ms) * 1000000); return 0; }
+// A poll nobody can be woken for: an empty set, or descriptors this service does not manage. POSIX waits the
+// timeout and an endless wait is endless — answering 0 after a 100 ms slice reads as a timeout the caller never
+// asked for, and a transport that arms itself on it spins instead of sleeping (the same shape as the two paths
+// below, and the third place it was hiding).
+static int sk_idle(int64_t ms) {
+    if (ms < 0) {
+        for (;;) {
+            if (dm_teardown_is_parking()) { dm_teardown_check_current_thread(); return 0; }
+            dm_guest_sleep_ns(1000000);
+        }
+    }
+    dm_guest_sleep_ns(ms * 1000000);
+    return 0;
+}
 typedef struct { int32_t fd; int16_t events, revents; } sk_pollfd;
 
 enum { EFD_MAX = 64, SK_POLLIN = 1, SK_POLLOUT = 4, SK_POLLRDNORM = 0x40, SK_POLLWRNORM = 4, SK_POLLHUP = 0x10, SK_POLLNVAL = 0x20,
